    "summary": "Cloth/skirt composed of 7 narrow strips hand-sewn together along the selvedges. The cloth is hand-woven from hand-spun cotton used in both warp and weft that has been dyed a uniform shade of indigo. One strip has been left undecorated, while the other six, after being sewn together, have been hand-embroidered using imported European thread coloured red, yellow and blue, with patterns of diamonds, square boxes and zig-zag lines that run across the cloth. At both ends there is a long fringe of indigo tassels which appear to have been braided from the loose warp ends.",
